# Golden fixtures are byte-exact artifacts. Git must never translate their line
# endings on checkout or commit: a CRLF rewrite would silently change what a
# vector tests (contracts/export-format.md EX-3 makes CR non-conforming, and
# vector 042-crlf deliberately CONTAINS a CR). -text disables all conversion.
#
# The SHA-256 manifest in contracts/fixtures/MANIFEST.sha256 is the detection
# half of this; -text is the prevention half. Both are needed — a manifest alone
# turns a mangled checkout into a confusing CI failure on every platform, and
# -text alone would not notice deliberate corruption.
contracts/fixtures/** -text
